prehistoric|PASS: Before written history and museum tools support tiền sử, with no invented date or claim that all regions began history simultaneously. Regional-period note is qualified; source-only adjective and Vietnamese river location are preserved.
sew|PASS: Needle/thread joining and apron-pocket attachment support khâu/may. Onto accurately identifies attachment. Sewed and sewn/sewed participles are correct; the note allows hand and machine sewing without falsely defining it as embroidery alone.
yellow|PASS: Attributive ribbon colour and uncountable paint colour distinguish the two Oxford POS boundaries. Vietnamese vàng and xanh lá retain both colours. Yellowish is an appropriate degree contrast; no colour-identity merge is authorized.
double|REVIEW: [POS_CLASSIFICATION] All five source ordinals are represented: two-part door adjective, noun-followed quantity determiner, standalone twelve-tool quantity pronoun, membership-change verb and paid-double adverb. Vietnamese preserves each construction. Det/pronoun/adverb taxonomy boundaries need owner review despite source support; accessible Oxford adjective/adverb and published wordlist extracts corroborate usage but do not approve canonical POS.
etiquette|PASS: Setting-specific politeness rules and formal dining introduction fit phép lịch sự. Vietnamese retains before-meal timing. Uncountability and culture/setting qualification avoid treating one dining convention as a universal moral rule.
